 [{:id :observe :defines :o :node :R2 :class :stack-defined :ref :friston2017
   :imports [:world]
   :formal "o_t <- structured observation of the world after action u_{t-1}"
   :lean "machineObservation" :lean-status :closed
   :lean-note "CARRIER DECLARED 2026-09-05 by :F8 leg 1 slice 5 (this row previously carried NO :lean and NO :lean-status at all -- it was one of the six class-(a) rows the rendered join printed as '--' rather than 'missing'). mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/MachineObservation.lean declares machineObservation as the construction the implementation runs (observe, observation.clj:103-146, paired with the tagged envelope observation-envelope builds at :85-101), and MachineObservationWitness.lean measures it against production (runs/F8-observe/clojure-readback.txt: fourteen coordinates at delta 0.0 on empty data, delta 0.0 on both clamped channels at and above cap, and delta 0.0 on all three unbounded cases). Both modules elaborate with 0 errors and 0 warnings; #print axioms on all 42 declarations gives [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], no sorryAx. THIS ROW IS :class :stack-defined AND ITS :formal LINE IS A BOUNDARY, NOT A FORMULA, so unlike slices 1-4 there is no equation to transcribe. What is stated instead is the CONSTRUCTION and the three claims it makes about itself. One holds and two do not, and both failures are exhibited rather than assumed away. (1) THE [0,1] BOUND IS ASSERTED IN FOUR PLACES AND ENFORCED AT TWO CHANNELS. observation.clj says the vector is in [0,1] at the namespace level (:5-7), on every one of the fourteen channel lines (:18-32), and in observe's own docstring (:105-106). In the body exactly two channels are clamped, both from above only -- :sorry-count-norm by (min 1.0 ...) at :133 and :coupling-density by (min 1.0 ...) at :136-137 -- and no channel is clamped from below. MEASURED AT HEAD: {:graph {:dynamics {:commit-percentages {:stack 70.0}}}} gives :stack-pct 70.0; {:loop-health {:overall -3.0}} gives :loop-health -3.0; and {:graph {:summary {:active-repos 20 :total-repos 4}}} gives :active-repo-ratio 5.0, which is the one that is not a pass-through -- observe COMPUTES that quotient at :129-132 and never checks the denominator against the numerator. So Holes.ObservationVector's value : Channel -> R is the honest carrier: BoundedObservation is stated as a PREDICATE that an observation may or may not satisfy, clampedChannelsAreBoundedAbove proves the bound holds at the two clamped channels for every raw reading, stackPctIsNotClamped shows the same construction passes the other twelve through, and the three measured values above are the three counterexamples. A bounded carrier would have stated a guarantee the machine does not make. (2) THE ABSENCE ENVELOPE PROMISES A COERCION ONE CHANNEL CANNOT PERFORM. channel-statuses writes {:variant :absent :reason :source-field-missing :paths [...] :coerced-to 0.0} at every absent channel unconditionally (:69-73). For thirteen channels that is what happens. For :active-repo-ratio it is not: its requirement paths include [:graph :summary :total-repos] (:57-58) but observe reads (:total-repos summary) at :129 WITH NO DEFAULT, so (pos? nil) raises. MEASURED: (observe {:graph {:summary {:active-repos 3}}}) throws java.lang.NullPointerException at observation.clj:129. THE EVIDENCE THAT THIS IS AN OVERSIGHT AND NOT A DESIGN IS ONE CHARACTER WIDE: :coupling-density reads the SAME KEY at :134 as (:total-repos summary 0), with a default, and coerces to 0.0 exactly as the envelope promises. In Lean the promise and its keeping are separated -- EnvelopePromises holds as written, PromiseKept fails, and incompleteActiveRepoSummaryBreaksTheCoercionPromise is the conjunction; activeRepoReading and couplingDensityReading are the two sides of the one-character difference. AND THE COUPLING SIDE IS NOT OBSERVABLE THROUGH observe: the same input that would exercise :coupling-density's default raises at :active-repo-ratio first, so ONE channel's missing default makes the other thirteen coordinates unobservable on that input, and the readback measures that refusal rather than a value. (observe {}) does NOT throw -- summary is nil and the (and summary ...) guard short-circuits -- so the crash needs a :summary map present and incomplete, which is why the six existing tests do not see it (their sample-data carries a complete summary, observation_test.clj:31-35, and their empty case carries no :graph at all, :95-99). (3) THE TWO CLAIMS THAT DO HOLD. The observation is TOTAL over Channel -- observe returns a literal fourteen-key map (:120-145), so (observe {}) gives 0.0 at all fourteen and no channel is ever missing. And sense->vector REFUSES to produce the ordered numeric vector unless the caller hands it the exact matching envelope (:148-158), which is what keeps absence provenance attached at a boundary where EDN metadata would drop it. In Lean the refusal is a SIGNATURE, not a theorem: senseToVector takes the matching proof as an argument, so the vector is unconstructible without it. THE REVIEW'S SHARPEST FINDING, and the reason this row's :lean-at names two shas. The first draft defined EnvelopeMatches as equality of the numeric coordinates alone. But sense->vector recomputes the whole tagged envelope and compares it entire (:152-156), and THE REFUSAL THE READBACK MEASURES IS A VARIANT MISMATCH AT IDENTICAL COORDINATES: the empty observation's envelope and the envelope of {:loop-health {:overall 0.0}} agree at all fourteen numeric coordinates -- both are 0.0 everywhere -- and differ only in :loop-health's variant (:absent with :reason :source-field-missing vs :observed). A value-only match test would have accepted exactly the pair under measurement. EnvelopeMatches now compares variant and value together, and readbackRefusalPairAgreesNumerically and readbackRefusalPairIsRefused are the two halves. THREE OTHER REVIEW REPAIRS, all at mathlib4 a4c2276d51. senseToVectorRequiresMatchingEnvelope was P -> P with the hypothesis as its own proof -- the shape the slice-4 review deleted at d7a45a358a -- and is gone. CoercionPromise was declared and never used, with finding (2) encoded as a fact about Option.isSome that mentioned no channel. upperClamp was tied to no channel, so nothing stated WHICH channels are clamped, and sorryAtCap and couplingAtCap were the same proposition under two names. NOT A RULING -- nothing is written to :choices. NOT REPAIRED ON PURPOSE: observation.clj is untouched. The [0,1] gap and the :active-repo-ratio crash are STATED here and left standing, because repairing them is a change to the machine and this is a leg-1 'state it in Lean' slice; they are carried as findings for a subsequent I-track item, not fixed under this row. NOT CLAIMED: nothing about what the operator's turns should mean in the observation (the PROBLEMS-r2-r8-r7-batch2.md :both item, :36-41), nothing about the eight-of-fourteen likelihood coverage that :prediction-error's row records, and no live tick was run. THIS ROW STILL CARRIES NO :code: it had none before this slice and the C522 sweep counted it among the six rows that make no pointer claim; the runtime sites are named in this note instead, as slice 4 did."
   :lean-at "mathlib4 a4c2276d51 (MachineObservation.lean, MachineObservationWitness.lean; the reviewed state, first committed at 169662b196 by codex-9)"}
  {:id :prediction-error :defines :eps :node :R8 :class :theory-defined :ref :buckley2017
   :imports [:o :mu]
   :formal "eps_k := o_k - mu_k" :eq "buckley2017 eq. 45 error terms (reduction: no generalised coordinates)" :lean "machineChannelPredictionError" :lean-status :closed
   :lean-note "CARRIER DECLARED 2026-09-05 by :F8 leg 1 slice 2 (this row previously read :lean nil :lean-status :missing). mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/MachinePredictionError.lean declares machineChannelPredictionError as the producer the implementation runs (free_energy.clj:203-278, compute-prediction-error under :prediction-error/v1), and MachinePredictionErrorWitness.lean proves eight scored reference values and five typed outcomes, every one matching production EXACTLY (runs/F8-prediction-error/clojure-readback.txt, delta 0.0 on all eight scored, 5/5 typed). Both modules elaborate with 0 errors and 0 warnings and #print axioms gives [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] on all 50 declarations, no sorryAx. THE :formal LINE ABOVE IS NOT THE WHOLE PRODUCER, and three reductions it does not carry are stated in Lean rather than in prose. (1) THE PRODUCER IS NOT A FUNCTION INTO R. It returns one of three typed records -- present, absent, refused -- and which one it returns is the decision (AC1, Joe 2026-09-02 on C130 s2). refusalDominatesAbsence: an unobserved channel whose likelihood ALSO failed is REFUSED, not omitted, so a tick's omission count is not its count of unobserved channels; absence_requires_wellFormedModel is the converse. (2) THE SUBTRACTED TERM IS NOT mu. It is :predicted-mean, a member of the likelihood output belief/predict-observation computes from the belief state (belief.clj:1199-1238); the implementation's belief is an entity-indexed CATEGORICAL map, not the per-channel Channel -> R mean this :formal line and Holes.BeliefState both assume, and the per-channel mean is a READOUT of it (belief.clj:640-737). registryFormOfPresent states exactly where this line holds: on a channel whose predicted mean IS the belief mean. Whether that holds of the running stack is a question about predict-observation and is NOT claimed here. (3) A REFUSAL OF ONE CHANNEL REFUSES THE WHOLE UPDATE (war_machine.clj:6110-6127): an absent channel is omitted and the rest are scored, but a single refusal empties the error map for every channel (oneRefusalEmptiesTheUpdate); and eps is attempted on only the EIGHT channels with a likelihood model (belief.clj:933-934), the other six producing no record at all (channelsWithoutLikelihood, verified equal to the Clojure set by the readback). THE FINDING, PROVED NOT ASSERTED: A NEGATIVE PREDICTED VARIANCE IS SCORED, NOT REFUSED. prediction-member (free_energy.clj:191-201) checks FINITENESS and not sign, so -4.0 is :present; the max at :270 then floors it to min-variance, giving the LARGEST per-call precision the floor allows (100 under the declared default) and a record indistinguishable from one built on a variance of exactly zero except by reading :predicted-variance back out (negativeVarianceIsNotRefused, subMinVarianceIsFloored, zeroAndNegativeVarianceAgree). A SECOND FINDING, THE ONE LEG 2 WILL CONSUME: the :precision this producer stamps is 1/max(predicted-variance, min-variance), derived from the LIKELIHOOD's variance for this one call, and is NOT R7's Pi, which is derived from the channel's ERROR HISTORY. They occupy the same :precision key at different points in one tick -- precision/weighted-error (precision.clj:213-233) overwrites the first with the second and preserves it as :per-call-precision. Measured on one channel in one tick (readback section 3): the producer stamps 4.0 and weighted-error 2.0; after the overwrite the same keys read 1.6 and 0.8, and 1.6 is 8/5, MachinePrecisionWitness.halfError from slice 1. The Lean module therefore names its field perCallPrecision: spelling it precision would reproduce the bare-symbol collision leg 2's concordance checker exists to refuse. NOT A RULING -- nothing is written to :choices, and no claim is made about whether the producer should refuse a negative variance or whether the two precisions should share a key. NOT CLAIMED: nothing about generalised coordinates (the reduction :eq already names), nothing about the R3 belief-aggregation driver that consumes these errors, nothing about :policy-free-energy, a different row on the same node. POINTER DEFECT FOUND HERE, REPAIRED BY THE LATER SWEEP: when this slice ran, :code read war_machine.clj:4368-4379, which at futon2 HEAD is inside scan-blocks, the Block-footer commit scanner, and has nothing to do with eps. The producer is free_energy.clj:203-278 and the tick's call site is war_machine.clj:6110-6127. This slice named the defect and left the field alone because :code is what TN 9a gates and no quantity slice owned it; the :F8 leg-1 :code sweep of 2026-09-05 (C522) read every :code range in this registry against HEAD and wrote those sites in."
   :lean-at "mathlib4 1282b75e32 (MachinePredictionError.lean, MachinePredictionErrorWitness.lean; parent e2e8ee9649, slice 1's sha)"
   :code "free_energy.clj:203-278 (compute-prediction-error, the typed triple), free_energy.clj:280-296 (channel-prediction-error); war_machine.clj:6110-6127 (the tick's per-channel call, the omission/refusal split, and the errors map it produces)"}
