   :lean-note "CARRIER DECLARED 2026-09-05 by :F8 leg 1 slice 7 (this row previously carried NO :lean and NO :lean-status at all -- one of the four class-(a) rows left after slice 6). mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/MachineDepth.lean declares machineDepth and MachineDepthWitness.lean discharges every hypothesis on concrete witnesses; production is measured in runs/F8-depth/clojure-readback.txt. THE CARRIER'S TYPE IS THE FINDING: machineDepth is Option Nat -> EfeDepths, not a number. The :formal line asks for ONE range for the sums in Q(o|pi) and G, and what the machine has is a map from the requested :horizon-steps to the FOUR depths its four G terms are evaluated at. efeDepths is its inhabitant. THE :formal LINE IS FALSE AS WRITTEN, and the failure is inside a single evaluation of G. next-mean is the depth-K final-state observation when the multi path runs, but next-var is ALWAYS the FIRST step's variance (efe.clj:633-636). So risk (efe.clj:641, through fe-on-predicted on next-mean) and homeostatic pressure (:706) sit at depth K while ambiguity (:701) and the predictability bonus (:705) sit at depth 1. gTermsDisagreeOnDepth states the disagreement as one proposition. MEASURED at HEAD on a stressed state (:sorry-count-norm 0.85, :mission-health 0.2, action {:type :address-sorry :target :m1}), K=1 vs K=3: G-risk moves -2.4115244739422366 and homeostatic-pressure -0.23999999999999994, while G-ambiguity and predictability-bonus move EXACTLY 0.0. Two terms follow the horizon and two are frozen at depth one, in the same call. THE EPISTEMIC HALF OF G HAS NO tau-SUM AT ALL, and this is structural rather than a consequence of the >= 2 guard. predict computes its variance as (predict-effects nil action) -- forward_model.clj:334 passes nil where the state would go -- and every :obs-variance arm is a literal keyed by action type (:138, :148, :165, :172, :184, :193, :202). So a constant-action rollout carries the SAME variance at every step: MEASURED, step-3 variance equals step-