   :measurement-that-separates-them "THE ARMS SEPARATE ON WHETHER O4 BECOMES EXERCISABLE, NOT ON WHETHER IT BECOMES TRUE -- no arm produces a true O4 at the denominator the gate grades. Arm A moves the carrying count 1 -> 2 and leaves the primary verdict false with zero contending primary rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:2, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:5, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:12); arm B moves the status :not-exercised -> :exercised-false (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:136, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:15); arm C leaves zero (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:246). THE ONE PLANT THAT DOES MOVE THE PRIMARY VERDICT TO TRUE IS A NEGATIVE CONTROL, NOT AN ARM: broadening an existing member-carried rule so it is live on primary rounds gives :primary-o4-true (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:256-259, planted at holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:160-165), and it is in the control set precisely because it is the edit that would make the law pass. So on everything measured, D3 and D2 are not independent: an affirmative D3 buys a TRUE O4 only if D2 also reads the law off a denominator wider than primary, where arm B gives true three times over (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:119, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:285, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:615). Three further controls fix what each measurement is sensitive to, each plant read back before its worker ran (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:35-40, hard-failing at holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:210-216): renaming the fifth rule to a nonmember returns O4 to :not-exercised (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:248-251), killing its antecedent takes i